} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/493"} "Auditorio Nacional, Ciudad de México"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/70336"} "101 from 24 countries"]]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Referee"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/28624"} "Valéria Nagy-Herpich"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HUN.png"}] "HUN"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The format was the same as in 1964, with the best six gymnasts in the individual all-around advancing to the apparatus final, with the final apparatus score made up of 50% of the all-around total and a final optional program. This was the only women’s individual event in Mexico City that was not won by " [:a {:href "/athletes/29115"} "Věra Čáslavská"] ", who eventually finished second. The gold went to Soviet " [:a {:href "/athletes/29195"} "Nataliya Kuchinskaya"] ", who had won the event at the 1966 World Championships, along with two other apparatus gold medals. Bronze went to Kuchinskaya’s teammate Belarussian " [:a {:href "/athletes/29207"} "Larisa Petrik"] ", who also won a gold medal on floor exercise in 1968, shared with Čáslavská. Fourth-place was a tie between East German " [:a {:href "/athletes/28502"} "Karin Janz"] " and American " [:a {:href "/athletes/29264"} "Linda Metheny"] ", whose fourth-place finish was the best in an individual gymnastics event at the Olympics by an American woman prior to the 1984 Olympics."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/29195"} "Nataliya Kuchinskaya"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-cent